Begin3
Title:          SHSUCD Suite
Version:        3-7
Entered-date:   2022-09-22
Description:    The SHSUCD suite is a set of programs dealing with the CD-ROM.
Summary:        The SHSUCD suite is a set of programs dealing with the CD-ROM. They allow access to the CD-ROM as a normal drive letter; create an image file from the contents of a CD-ROM; access an image file as a drive; and test certain CD-ROM functions. These drivers are installed to a DRIVERS directory to prevent a conflict with the SHSUCDX package provided with FreeDOS.
Keywords:       mscdex, shsucdex, fdcdex, cdrom, atapicdd, xcdrom, shsucdx, shsucdhd, shsucdrd, shsudvhd, shsucdri, omi, isobar, cdtest, smarter
Author:         John H. McCoy
Maintained-by:  Jason Hood <jadoxa -at- yahoo.com.au>
Primary-site:   http://adoxa.altervista.org/shsucdx/index.html
Previous-site:  http://www.geocities.com/jadoxa/shsucdx/index.html
Alternate-site: http://www.ibiblio.org/pub/micro/pc-stuff/freedos/files/dos/shsucdx/
Original-site:  http://www.shsu.edu/~csc_jhm/
Defunct-Original-site: http://www.pfu.net/fedtech/fcdex/ (no longer online)
Platforms:      DOS (NASM), FreeDOS
Copying-policy: Open Source (copyright reserved, free use program)
end
